in the days of Rehoboam. We have on record two of his remarkable prophecies, 1 Kings 11:31-39, announcing the rending of the ten tribes from Solomon; and 1 Kings 14:6-16, delivered to Jeroboam’s wife, foretelling the death of Abijah the king’s son, the destruction of Jeroboam’s house, and the captivity of Israel “beyond the river.”","verses":11,"father":"","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"iddo_1594","name":"Iddo","also":"","summary":"Lovely. A prophet of Judah who wrote the history of Rehoboam and Abijah (2 Chr. 12:15).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[31]},{"id":"rehoboam_2412","name":"Rehoboam","also":"Roboam","summary":"He enlarges the people, the successor of Solomon on the throne, and apparently his only son. He was the son of Naamah “the Ammonitess,” some well-known Ammonitish princess (1 Kings 14:21; 2 Chr. 12:13).","verses":42,"father":"Solomon","mother":"Naamah","v":[31]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,25,27,30]},{"id":"sheba_1067","name":"Sheba","kind":"Region","lat":9.02274,"lon":38.7468,"summary":"Heb. id. A kingdom in Arabia Felix. Sheba, in fact, was Saba in Southern Arabia, the Sabaeans of classical geography, who carried on the trade in spices with the other peoples of the ancient world.","verses":17,"v":[1,3,9,12]},{"id":"ophir_911","name":"Ophir","kind":"Region","lat":27.5,"lon":67.5,"summary":"Some region famous for its gold (1 Kings 9:28; 10:11; 22:48; Job 22:24; 28:16; Isa. 13:12). In the LXX. this word is rendered “Sophir,” and “Sofir” is the Coptic name for India, which is the rendering of the Arabic version, as also of the Vulgate.","verses":10,"v":[10]},{"id":"arabia_80","name":"Arabia","kind":"Region","lat":27.4,"lon":37.7,"summary":"Arabia Petraea, i.e., the Rocky Arabia, so called from its rocky mountains and stony plains. It comprehended all the north-west portion of the country, and is much better known to travellers than any other portion.","verses":6,"v":[14]},{"id":"lebanon_585","name":"Lebanon","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"White, “the white mountain of Syria,” is the loftiest and most celebrated mountain range in Syria. It is a branch running southward from the Caucasus, and at its lower end forking into two parallel ranges, the eastern or Anti-Lebanon, and the western or Lebanon proper.","verses":5,"v":[16,20]},{"id":"tarshish_1139","name":"Tarshish","kind":"","lat":36.953,"lon":-6.37934,"summary":"The name of a place which first comes into notice in the days of Solomon. The question as to the locality of Tarshish has given rise to not a little discussion.","verses":20,"v":[21]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[26,28]},{"id":"euphrates_421","name":"Euphrates","kind":"Water (River)","lat":34.74942,"lon":40.9364,"summary":"Hebrew, Perath; Assyrian, Purat; Persian cuneiform, Ufratush, whence Greek Euphrates, meaning “sweet water.” The Assyrian name means “the stream,” or “the great stream.”","verses":32,"v":[26]},{"id":"shephelah_1074","name":"Shephelah","kind":"Region","lat":31.75,"lon":34.75,"summary":"region","verses":6,"v":[27]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[4436,4436,4436,4436,7614,7614,8085,853,8088,8088,8010,8010,935,935,5254,5254,8010,2420,2420,2420,3389,3389,3389,3389,3966,3966,